  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the mirror image $Q$ when the point $P(3,1)$ is reflected in the line $y=2x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$Q(-1,3)$.\n\nThe perpendicular meets the mirror line at $M(1,2)$; repeat the displacement from $P$ to $M$.",
      "worked": "The perpendicular through $P$ has gradient $-\\frac12$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=-\\frac12(x-3)\\\\2y-2&=-x+3\\\\x+2y&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nAt its intersection $M$ with $y=2x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2(2x)&=5\\\\5x&=5\\\\x&=1\\\\y&=2(1)\\\\y&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $M(1,2)$. From $P$ to $M$ the displacement is two units left and one unit up. Repeat this displacement from $M$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x_Q&=1-2=-1\\\\y_Q&=2+1=3.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $Q(-1,3)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 126
  },
